ob involves any kind of  education component  so i just kind of you know spit off the  name of like half a dozen packages  and you're probably like oh my god  there's so many different packages to  learn  but kind of one of the bright sides is  just like how  if you kind of learn the basic syntax of  the tidy verse  is that kind of allows you to easily  extend that into other related packages  like tidy models and ggplot the exact  same is true for our markdown  once and i would argue it's even  actually much easier once you have the  basic syntax of our markdown again as i  mentioned  um you can create things in chunks and  there's various options as to what you  can do if you want to show or hide  code or plots etc and once you're  familiar with kind of the basic syntax  of our markdown  that means it's very easy to all you  have to do is again learn kind of the  specific details about the various  output formats in the packages  but it's really much very easy to just  take whatever your analysis work is  and easily make that into different  output formats whether that's an html  file you want to share with a teammate  or you know a set of slides to make a  presentation to show to someone higher  up which of course wouldn't have code  but would probably have some plots that  you know resulted from that code and so  you don't have to duplicate  that work um so i hope again  it was difficult to distill all of my  love for our mark down into  10-ish minutes but i hope that you are  either inspired to  include our markdown to start including  our markdown as a part of your workflow  or if we are if you already use our  markdown a little bit like maybe you  work  you kind of do your personal analysis in  our markdown documents which is a great  start  is that you realize kind of how much  knowledge you already have and you can  really easily extend those capabilities  into other formats and create slides and  websites etc  and so i've included a few links here uh  thes